# S12.1 CI diagnosis: recovery barrier path scope

## Failure

CI run `36486243677` failed only in the new recovery-barrier test. The
unprivileged runner rejected a cross-directory exchange involving a mode-`000`
guard.

## Cause

The first reviewed correction placed quarantined Git metadata in the repository
parent to keep it away from `git clean`. That cross-directory placement was
unnecessary and reduced portability of the atomic exchange primitive.

## Versioned correction

The guard and quarantined Git directory now exchange atomically in the same
repository directory. Every recovery `git clean` carries an exact exclusion for
the fixed quarantine name, and the focused test executes both the writer block
and the clean-with-exclusion path.

No server mutation or deployment attempt occurred.
